```
This code registers a new block type called `custom-block/block` with a title, description, and a render callback function `render_custom_block`.

3. Create a new PHP file in the same directory as `custom-block.php`, for example, `block.php`. This file will contain the render callback function `render_custom_block`.
```php
<?php
function render_custom_block( $attributes, $content, $block ) {
    $heading = $attributes['heading'];
    $paragraph = $attributes['paragraph'];
    $image_url = $attributes['image'];

    $image = wp_get_attachment_image( $image_url, 'full' );

    return sprintf(
        '<div class="custom-block">%s%s%s</div>',
        '<h2>' . $heading . '</h2>',
        '<p>' . $paragraph . '</p>',
        $image
    );
}
```
This function takes the block attributes, content, and block object as arguments, and returns the rendered HTML for the block.

